we want to talk about an important issue  happening right here in town the rise of  fentanyl in las vegas  jamie ross the executive director at pac  coalition is joining us to tell more hey  jamie how are you  doing well how are you i can't complain  but i do want to talk about what's  happening right now with the opioid  crisis  in las vegas so unfortunately we are  seeing a rise in  fentanyl overdoses um the first  uh time i think anyone heard about  opioids was when we were talking about  prescription opioids  uh and we did a really good job of  changing the laws and changing the  social norms around prescription opioids  uh and then so we saw those numbers go  down and then we saw the heroin numbers  go up and we've worked really hard  for the heroin numbers to go down and  now  unfortunately what we're seeing is  fentanyl  numbers and fentanyl overdoses go up  significantly  so what is what is fentanyl and then why  is it so dangerous  so fentanyl is uh it's a synthetic  opioid drug  so think prescription opioids like  oxycontin and  percocet and then but it is  50 times more powerful than heroin uh  and  so the issue is what we're seeing is  it's coming across the border in pressed  pills  that look a lot like oxycontin percocet  etc and they're being sold on the black  market and of course there is  no quality control whatsoever and with  no quality control you don't know what  you're getting  and what we know about fentanyl is  it is an incredibly dangerous drug um  and it's the difference between trying  to smuggle  over an entire salt shaker versus a  couple of grains of salt  and we've got less than 30 seconds here  i do want to ask a person talk about  narcan  what is narcan and how is this involved  with fentanyl  so narcan is an overdose reversal drug  uh and the important thing about narcan  is  if you suspect an opioid overdose you  can give  narcan with almost no side effects but  you also have to call 9-1-1 that's the  most important thing  is call 9-1-1 and if you need access to  narcan  uh please visit our website which is  drug free las vegas dot org  and you can access anywhere to get free  narcan  in all of nevada super helpful stuff  jamie thank you so much for joining us  for more information  call pac coalition at 702 582-pac  or find them online at  drugfreelasvegas.org
 

